<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kontagora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kontagora was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> and town in present-day north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. It was among the first emirates conquered by British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a>, falling in 1900. Its fall began the systematic British campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s emirates that ended Sokoto's independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kontagora.jpg" alt="Kontagora" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kambai Akau · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagwamatse_roundabout_in_Kontagora_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
